<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lille</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rijsel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lille is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> near the Belgian border, historically the chief town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walloon-flanders">Walloon Flanders</a>. Part of the County of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a> and later the Burgundian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xiv">Louis XIV</a> in 1667 and became French by the Treaty of Aix-la-Chapelle in 1668, after which Vauban built its citadel. It became a great centre of the textile industry and is the capital of the Hauts-de-France region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lille.jpg" alt="Lille" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cereol89, Velvet · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lille_Collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
